  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Construction of a front porch including relocation of the side entrance door to the front and the partial demolition of the existing rear extension",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed porch, by reason of its scale, design and siting, would result in an awkward and incongruous addition that sits uncomfortably within the front elevation of the property. It would harm the established rhythm of the terrace, appear visually jarring and unduly prominent, and would disrupt the symmetry of the terrace row, resulting in poor overall design quality.&nbsp;It therefore fails to respect the character and appearance of the site and surrounding area including the Becontree Estate which is a non-designated heritage asset, causing harm to each of these including to the historic distinctiveness of the area.&nbsp;The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG) (December, 2025)Policies D4 and&nbsp;HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
